course: dictionary
lesson: 11225
title: Woody: wood-like, hard and full of trees
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Woody comes from wood, the hard material inside trees. Words ending in -y often mean full of or like something. Woody means made of wood, or like wood. «A tree is a large plant with a woody trunk.» The trunk is hard like wood, not soft and green like grass.
explain: Use the words around woody to choose the right meaning. «Grapes grow on a woody climbing vine» tells you the vine has a hard, stiff stem, because it climbs and is pruned each winter. A woody hillside is a hill with lots of trees. Ask: is this plant or place made of wood, or full of trees?
explain: Woody can also describe a taste or smell. If a drink tastes woody, it tastes like wood. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of woody. If it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Woody means made of wood, like wood, or full of trees.
fact: Woody plants, such as trees and bushes, have hard stems; herbs and grass have soft green stems.
fact: «A tree is a large plant with a woody trunk.» Each year it grows a new layer of wood under its bark.
fact: That yearly layer shows as a ring when a tree is cut across.
fact: «Grapes grow on a woody climbing vine.» Raisins and sultanas are dried grapes.
exercise: In «A tree is a large plant with a woody trunk», what does woody describe? | The colour of the sky | *The hard, wood-like trunk | A quick sound | The soft leaves
exercise: Which of these is a woody plant? | Lettuce | Basil herb | *An oak tree | Grass
exercise: Which phrase means a place with lots of trees? | A sandy beach | A frozen lake | *A woody hillside
test: Which one describes a woody taste or smell? | Cold like ice | *Like freshly cut timber | Sweet like sugar | Salty like the sea
test: What does each ring in a cut tree show? | The tree's name | *One year of growth | A bird's nest
exam: «Grapes grow on a woody climbing vine.» What does woody tell you about the vine? | *Its stem is hard, like wood | It grows in water | Its stem is soft and green | It has no leaves
